  "narrative": "No new validation supports acceptance of any claim as clinically meaningful in this dataset. For the due H4 deadline, feature_002=1 versus 0 on outcome_006 had direction -1, so positive signed estimates correspond to more negative raw scores, i.e. stronger dependency. Discovery R4 was signed +0.0209 with a wide interval crossing zero, while independent validation R13 reversed to -0.0123 and its conservative validation interval also crossed zero and spanned the approximate 10% scale for outcome_006. The split-level disagreement and lack of a conservative interval above the clinical threshold argue against a robust association; H4 is rejected and closed. For H37, feature_065=1 versus 0 on outcome_015 was the only feature_065 candidate remaining: discovery R27 was signed +0.0211 [0.0018, 0.0404], excluding zero but lying below the approximate 10% absolute threshold for outcome_015 and including negligible effects in its lower half. Validation R39 reversed to -0.00825 [-0.0365, 0.0200] under the conservative validation alpha, crossing zero and not supporting the hypothesized direction. Together with the failed outcome_012 validation and the null/opposite cross-outcome feature_065 screen, this closes feature_065 as a clinically meaningful predictor. For H5, feature_034=1 versus 0 on outcome_006 had direction +1. Discovery R5 was negative and interval-crossing, while validation R40 was positive with point estimate above the approximate 10% threshold for outcome_006 but with a conservative interval that still crosses zero. Because the two splits disagree in direction and the validation uncertainty is not sufficient to support a clear clinically meaningful difference, H5 remains a negative/inconsistent signal and is rejected and closed. At this point the scientifically meaningful supported findings are none: the data provide negative evidence for feature_065, feature_002, and feature_034 on the outcomes tested, as well as most prior binary and subgroup contrasts. The remaining unresolved uncertainty is mainly the still-untested registered screens on outcome_012 and outcome_015, plus untested outcomes. The most informative next analysis is to continue registered diversity screens and new broad screens on less-covered outcomes, accepting only estimates with intervals that clearly exceed the approximate 10% scale and show consistency. These remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted: none. H4 closed after validation sign reversal on outcome_006. H5 closed despite positive validation point estimate because discovery was opposite and conservative interval crossed zero. H37 closed after failed independent validation on outcome_015; do not chase feature_065 further. All feature_065 claims H16, H37-H44 are closed as not clinically meaningful. Do not re-open feature_002 or feature_034 on outcome_006 without a new pre-specified rationale; current evidence is split inconsistent and uncertain. Next analyze priorities: registered active outcome_012 screens H19, H20, H21, H23, H24, H27, H28, H29, H30, H33, H34, H36, and outcome_015 H48/H49, then broaden to under-covered outcomes. Acceptance requires intervals excluding zero and a point estimate/interval clearly at or above the approximate 10% outcome-scale threshold; interval-crossing trends should be rejected unless replication or a clearly clinically meaningful interval emerges. Avoid unique ID feature_003 and constant features feature_033/feature_049. Treat nominal categorical levels as nominal labels. All conclusions are dataset-specific, not causal or generalizable."
